                    },
                    "message": "This looks okay to me.  I'll leave it at +1 for a bit to allow others to provide feedback before promoting to +2."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Bills",
                        "email": "jason.m.bills@linux.intel.com",
                        "username": "jmbills"
                    },
                    "message": "It's been a couple of weeks with no additional feedback, so going ahead with +2."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/power_control.cpp",
                    "line": 2945,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Bills",
                        "email": "jason.m.bills@linux.intel.com",
                        "username": "jmbills"
                    },
                    "message": "This seems to rely on the fact that the postCompleteConfig.type enum class is zero-initialized, which looks like it is defined behavior from what I have found, so I think it should be okay.\n\nMy only hesitation is that this is different from how we handle the other optional signals where we check for the name to be empty such as on line 2963:\n```\nif (!nmiOutConfig.lineName.empty())\n```\n\nOtherwise, this does save the additional empty line check, so it's potentially more efficient.  So, I'm okay with this approach."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/power_control.cpp",
                    "line": 2945,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Bills",
                        "email": "jason.m.bills@linux.intel.com",
                        "username": "jmbills"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/power_control.cpp",
                    "line": 2945,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "yeah it seems to be defined behavior, and the way that this particular enum was setup, for better or worse. IMO, it would be nicer to have something like an \"isPresent\" method, but I didn't want to go change the whole file as I don't have access to a fully featured intel platform."
                }
            ],
